WEBVTT

00:00.800 --> 00:05.600
Last November, our Conduit automation rate was forty-one percent.

00:05.600 --> 00:08.330
In October, it hit ninety-two.

00:08.900 --> 00:10.500
How did we get there?

00:10.500 --> 00:12.740
With Claude Code and Codex,

00:12.740 --> 00:14.750
and one simple method.

00:15.320 --> 00:16.810
Measure the rate.

00:16.840 --> 00:20.450
Collect every conversation a person still handled.

00:20.520 --> 00:22.040
Find the cause.

00:22.040 --> 00:23.930
Fix the biggest group.

00:23.960 --> 00:26.210
Replay those cases as tests.

00:26.440 --> 00:27.250
Ship it.

00:27.400 --> 00:29.090
Then do it again.

00:29.660 --> 00:32.590
Each fix goes in the layer that owns it.

00:32.620 --> 00:34.790
A missing fact is knowledge.

00:35.020 --> 00:37.190
The wrong voice is the persona.

00:37.500 --> 00:39.350
A leak is a guardrail.

00:39.580 --> 00:42.430
A skipped step is a Conduit skill.

00:42.460 --> 00:44.310
Live data is a tool.

00:44.460 --> 00:47.750
And an agent that never ran is the runtime.

00:48.320 --> 00:52.210
The Conduit workspace skill teaches your agent this method.

00:52.240 --> 00:54.880
Ask it to raise your automation rate.

00:54.880 --> 00:57.040
It takes a read-only snapshot,

00:57.040 --> 00:59.800
measures, reads what people still handled,

00:59.800 --> 01:02.330
and fixes the biggest cause first.

01:02.900 --> 01:05.140
It follows your rules first.

01:05.140 --> 01:07.620
It snapshots before every change,

01:07.620 --> 01:12.110
never bulk-deletes knowledge, and keeps access codes out of prompts.

01:12.680 --> 01:14.760
It's free and open source.

01:14.760 --> 01:17.400
Install it in Claude Code or Codex,

01:17.400 --> 01:19.410
and point it at your workspace.
